# tests/IR_XFAIL — files that fail under --use-ir-codegen during M3 milestone.
#
# Format: one path per line, optional `# reason` after the path.
# Lines starting with `#` are comments. Blank lines ignored.
#
# When a file is removed from this list, the corresponding M3 PR has closed
# its parity gap. CI's test-ir job uses this to compute pass/fail:
#   - file in XFAIL + fails  → counted as xfail (OK)
#   - file in XFAIL + passes → "unexpected OK" (remove from XFAIL)
#   - file not in XFAIL + fails → unexpected failure (CI fails once gate is blocking)
#
# Validate this file with: bash scripts/check_ir_xfail.sh
#
# Closed gates (M3 milestone, in order):
#   PR 2 — CPR ctor lowering (boxed)              ✓ #47
#   PR 3 — TUnary `!` + `-`, binary `/`           ✓ #48
#   PR 4 — short-circuit `&&` / `||`              ✓ #49
#   PR 5 — top-level let bindings (module-init)   ✓ #50
#   PR 6 — top-level fn eta wrappers              ✓ #51
#   PR 7 — tuple expressions + TuplePattern       ✓ this PR
#   PR 8 — nested constructor patterns            ✓ this PR
#   PR 9 — String equality `==` / `!=`            ✓ this PR
#   PR 10 — Bool and Unit as i64 call args        ✓ this PR
#   PR 11 — do-block + IO + main body + Bool/Char ==  ✓ this PR — M3 corpus milestone closer
#            Cleared: hello, factorial, fizzbuzz, maybe_map, tuples, smoke_shapes 01/02/05
#   PR 13 — do-block Maybe wrapper-strip binding (Result deferred)  ✓ this PR
#            ast_to_ir now lowers `x <- f()` when f returns Maybe a !{IO} into a
#            sprout_tag → icmp → br i1 → (short Nothing / cont payload-extract) → phi
#            shape mirroring codegen.sprout's emit_do_maybe_bind.  Re-probe of the
#            4 example XFAILs (do_notation_demo, http_echo_server, http_get_cli,
#            io_result_do_demo) shows ast_to_ir now passes cleanly — all 4 now hit
#            the next-dominant blocker: extern-fn declarations not flowing into
#            the LLVM declare list (see ~4 entries below).
#
# Bucket breakdown after PR 13 closes (re-probed):
#   ~36 entries — @append undefined (typeclass Semigroup dispatch gap; pre-existing)
#   ~20 entries — @char_to_string undefined (Char literal / Char type ops not yet lowered)
#    ~6 entries — Char literal not yet supported (ast_to_ir TChar case)
#    ~4 entries — user `extern fn` declarations not emitted as LLVM `declare`
#                 (was masked by do-block Maybe/Result XFAIL until PR 13)
#    ~2 entries — multiple definition of local 't0' (codegen dup-block bug; pre-existing)
#    ~2 entries — pre-existing direct-codegen xfails (unresolved name in source)
#    Result wrapper-strip — separate follow-up, needs TCall ctor-name routing fix
#                 (Err/Ok ctors in helper bodies currently lower as `call @Err`).
#
# Dominant new blocker: @char_to_string / Char literal (TChar lowering) + @append (typeclass)

